From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] geolocation: positions from GeoClue2, consent, events (3555)

geolocation: Geolocator positions from GeoClue2, consent and events

GetGeopositionAsync (with and without age/timeout), PositionChanged and StatusChanged, and
Geolocator.RequestAccessAsync (new IGeolocatorStatics) are backed by GeoClue2 on the system D-Bus.
The unix side (geolocation.so, libdbus loaded with dlopen like powrprof/mountmgr) creates a GeoClue
client with DesktopId "wine" and the requested accuracy, starts it, reads Location (or waits for
LocationUpdated) and stops it. Geoposition/Geocoordinate/IReference<double>/event argument classes
are new; the async operations run on the thread pool.

Consent is the capability access ConsentStore "location" Value: HKLM (device), HKCU (user) and
HKCU\...\NonPackaged (desktop apps); Deny in any of them makes RequestAccessAsync return Denied,
GetGeopositionAsync fail with E_ACCESSDENIED, LocationStatus report Disabled, and GeoClue is never
contacted. It is read at every request. No GeoClue: status NotAvailable and the operation fails with
the timeout error. WINE_SG_GEOCLUE_BUS_ADDRESS redirects the bus for tests.
